assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

(testing process update 2026-07-10: the [scala unit] and [bridge]
cases below are now written as munit suites in the mcp_test/
component -- scala-unit cases in mcp_test/src/mcp_handler_tests.scala
over Fake_Backend, bridge cases in mcp_test/src/mcp_bridge_tests.scala
extending MCP_Session_Suite and its fixtures (with_repl, slow_step,
await_busy, eventually, expect_ok/expect_error); see plans/README
"testing process". run: isabelle mcp_test [-b] [-t PATTERN].)

T1  json number -> decimal string -> Value.parse_int survives the
    chain including negatives.
    test [scala unit]: tools/call with state_idx -1 -> fake saw
    ("state_idx", "-1"). (non-integer json number -> invalid params
    at the edge, never reaches the bridge.)
T2  index semantics match repl_state's: 0 = base, -1 = latest, out of
    range -> status error "out of range (0..n)".
    test [ml unit]: init, 2 steps; fork at 0 / 1 / -1 / 99 — first
    three ok (fork at -1 equals fork at 2), last is an error.
T3  duplicate new_repl id errors and changes nothing; parent stays
    steppable (claim released).
    test [ml unit]: fork onto an existing id -> error "already
    exists"; parent still steps.
T4  the fork is independent: stepping the fork does not change the
    parent's steps, and vice versa below the fork point.
    test [ml unit]: fork at -1, step the fork, show parent -> parent
    unchanged; step parent, show fork -> fork unchanged.
T5  orphan rule: truncating the parent strictly below the fork point
    removes the fork (and its descendants); a busy fork blocks the
    truncate.
    test [ml unit]: fork at state 2, truncate parent to 0 -> fork
    gone from repls. (busy-block is a bridge concern, covered in
    plans/repl_truncate T4.)
T6  full chain.
    test [bridge]: init, step, fork, step fork, repls shows both with
    origins.
    test [e2e]: fork -> merge round trip (with plans/repl_merge).

